WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.299 --> 00:00:01.656
When calculating a limit,

2
00:00:01.664 --> 00:00:03.299
if you obtain zero over zero,

3
00:00:03.413 --> 00:00:04.771
is the answer zero?

4
00:00:04.864 --> 00:00:07.253
No. This is an indeterminate form,

5
00:00:07.253 --> 00:00:09.380
a form that does not determine the result.

6
00:00:09.380 --> 00:00:10.695
Let me show you why.

7
00:00:11.002 --> 00:00:13.425
As x approaches zero from the right,

8
00:00:13.476 --> 00:00:15.196
x divided by x equals one.

9
00:00:15.268 --> 00:00:17.564
But x squared divided by x equals x,

10
00:00:17.615 --> 00:00:20.082
whose limit is zero. The same form,

11
00:00:20.111 --> 00:00:22.236
yet two different results.

12
00:00:22.458 --> 00:00:24.027
Now take a clear example.

13
00:00:24.205 --> 00:00:26.714
We want the limit of x squared minus four,

14
00:00:26.722 --> 00:00:28.143
divided by x minus two,

15
00:00:28.215 --> 00:00:29.814
as x approaches two.

16
00:00:30.093 --> 00:00:32.192
First, try substitution.

17
00:00:32.302 --> 00:00:35.302
The numerator is two squared minus four, or zero.

18
00:00:35.374 --> 00:00:38.118
The denominator is two minus two, also zero.

19
00:00:38.233 --> 00:00:40.059
This substitution cannot give the answer.

20
00:00:40.195 --> 00:00:42.205
Second, factor the numerator.

21
00:00:42.268 --> 00:00:44.444
x squared minus four is a difference

22
00:00:44.444 --> 00:00:47.572
of two squares. It equals x minus two

23
00:00:47.687 --> 00:00:49.258
multiplied by x plus two.

24
00:00:49.479 --> 00:00:51.455
Now cancel the common factor,

25
00:00:51.527 --> 00:00:54.235
x minus two, provided x

26
00:00:54.235 --> 00:00:56.531
is not equal to two. This is valid

27
00:00:56.539 --> 00:00:58.749
because in a limit, x approaches two.

28
00:00:58.757 --> 00:01:01.288
We do not need the function's value at exactly two.

29
00:01:01.551 --> 00:01:03.847
The remaining limit is that of x plus two.

30
00:01:03.983 --> 00:01:05.511
Calculate two plus two,

31
00:01:05.519 --> 00:01:08.071
which gives four. The limit is four,

32
00:01:08.079 --> 00:01:10.512
although the original function is undefined at two.

33
00:01:10.751 --> 00:01:13.069
Use the same idea for this exercise.

34
00:01:13.183 --> 00:01:14.925
x squared minus nine,

35
00:01:14.975 --> 00:01:16.695
divided by x minus three,

36
00:01:16.767 --> 00:01:18.701
as x approaches three.

37
00:01:18.773 --> 00:01:21.652
Factor, cancel, then calculate.

38
00:01:21.817 --> 00:01:22.890
The answer is six.
